# Fix: record live two-way calls as audio, not just transcript
#
# Evidence (call 2026-11-11 11:08 PST, record:
#   workspace/beagle-voice-agent/records/call-2026-11-11-1108-wei.md):
#   Wei asked (turn 6): "你把我們的對話…先record" — record our conversation.
#   What he got was transcript + timings only. The record itself states:
#   "no audio file is captured by the current stack — this transcript +
#   timing record is what exists".
#
# Root cause, verified in code: the live two-way path (converse.js ->
# lib/conversation.js ConversationSession) never taps the audio. The
# recording building blocks already exist in the same repo but only on
# the old one-way path: agent.js recordRemote() writes remote Opus RTP
# via lib/ogg.js OggOpusWriter and converts to WAV with lib/audio.js
# oggToWav (ffmpeg). converse.js creates ConversationSession for both
# inbound and outbound calls and never passes any recording option.
#
# Fix (one file changed in the live path, plus wiring + a test):
#   lib/conversation.js — ConversationSession gains optional
#     {recordDir, callId}. When set, it:
#     * writes the caller's raw Opus packets that pass the echo gate
#       (the packets VAD/ASR actually consume, not speakerphone echo
#       of Noor's own replies) to <recordDir>/call-<id>-wei.ogg, and
#       converts it to -wei.wav on close (existing oggToWav/ffmpeg);
#     * saves each of Noor's spoken replies (the Piper WAV the backend
#       already returns) to call-<id>-noor-turn<N>.wav;
#     * writes call-<id>.json: callId, peerId, started/endedAt,
#       receivedPackets, and per-turn {turn, transcript, language,
#       reply, file names}.
#     Recording failures are caught, logged, and never break a call;
#     with no recordDir nothing changes (existing tests construct the
#     session without it). An empty recording (0 packets) deletes the
#     .ogg and writes no manifest.
#   converse.js — passes recordDir=<agent>/records and the real callId
#     into both ConversationSession creations (inbound accept and
#     outbound onOutboundId), so the next call lands in records/
#     next to the transcript .md files.
#   tests/conversation.test.js — feeds a real WAV->Opus->decoder->VAD
#     pipeline through a recording session and asserts the .ogg, the
#     converted .wav, the per-turn reply wav, and the manifest exist.
#     Verified 2026-11-11 ~14:50 PST on a scratch copy: all 17 tests
#     in tests/conversation.test.js pass, including the new one.
#
# Apply:  cd ~/workspace/beagle-voice-agent && patch -p1 < fix-call-audio-recording.patch
#         (working tree is not a git repo, so no git apply)
# Then:   restart the listener (same restart as the hearing-grounding
#         patch — bundle both into one restart + one test call), make
#         a short call, and check records/ for call-<id>-wei.wav,
#         call-<id>-noor-turn1.wav and call-<id>.json.
# NOT fixed by this patch: 9.6-11.4 s turn latency, the 3 empty
#   transcripts, or the hearing-grounding defect (separate patch:
#   fix-hearing-grounding.patch). The .ogg/.wav is Wei's side only
#   post echo-gate plus Noor's replies as separate files — a mixed
#   single-track recording is a later step, not this one.
#
